From b9b460318a59a988c4e9d6dc3e2304875ae6418a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: REDACTED-AUTHOR <REDACTED-EMAIL>
Date: Sat, 27 Jun 2026 01:24:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] kmem: force DMA32 zone in __kfio_malloc (NUMA1 EB-scan buf
 <4GB)

task-10911: the EB-header scan buffer (ifio_c6e99 -> kfio_malloc) landed
>4GB on socket-1 cards; the 32-bit card could not write EB headers ->
corrupt read -> blob set disable flag (dev+0xed8) -> attach EINVAL.
Force __GFP_DMA32 so the buffer is physically <4GB.

NOTE: simple variant per lead order; if slab ignores __GFP_DMA32, fall
back to __get_free_pages(gfp|__GFP_DMA32) + size-header.

---
 root/usr/src/iomemory-vsl-3.2.16/kmem.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/root/usr/src/iomemory-vsl-3.2.16/kmem.c b/root/usr/src/iomemory-vsl-3.2.16/kmem.c
index 41101bb..94d9a52 100644
--- a/root/usr/src/iomemory-vsl-3.2.16/kmem.c
+++ b/root/usr/src/iomemory-vsl-3.2.16/kmem.c
@@ -61,7 +61,7 @@ static void *__kfio_malloc(fio_size_t size, gfp_t gfp, kfio_numa_node_t node)
 
     FUSION_ALLOCATION_TRIPWIRE_TEST();
 
-    return kmalloc(size, gfp);
+    return kmalloc(size, gfp | __GFP_DMA32);
 }
 
 /**
